oor parks  walkable neighborhoods  third places ability to support  different mobility devices  these are all ideas that thrive even a  new neighborhood we're designing  in san diego right now has the same  concepts very mixed use  ability to translate access to nature in  daylight  access to air ability to spatially be  distant  even when you're socially connected so  important right now  and all of these good design principles  with  digital infrastructure integrated make a  difference because they  allow us to shift between the physical  and digital as needed  in the end what we hope  this entire year has taught us is  three or four fundamental shifts one  we have realized that i'm not just  responsible for my health  i am responsible for your health and you  are responsible for mine  so we have to survive really  as a community we have to thrive as a  community  the shift from aesthetics to synthetics  we know how we experience  things matters the shift from physical  to digital and from physical to  physical there you realize that our  digital and physical  realities are integrated and most  importantly perhaps even as we go  through  all of these shifts and understand that  our  worlds are so intrinsically  interwoven that we are finally realizing  in 2020 that a purely human-centered  world  will not get us where we need to be we  have to shift from being  human-centered to living-centered  and think like an ecosystem  really celebrating differences  celebrating interdependencies and  understanding  that being a community gives us health  makes us resilient thank you  so much for your time
 

